::  name       tilak root count
::  shape      roots - int (@u32)
::  invariant  always two hardcoded engine roots: plain-bytes and manifest
::  example    2
::  readers    Pond - Amphora - Weave - Surface first resident
::  nib        surface-p11-v0
::
::  Surface Chapter p11 -- first resident in src/til.
::  Names the two Tilak roots from the marked-value brief; does not seat %tile
::  (held for Keaton). Thin +$ / $: one-field shape so the room opens honestly.
::
::  the roots the engine hardcodes, as amphora/manifest_entry.rye publishes them:
::    plain-bytes
::    manifest
::  that is the whole pair.
::
::  Why this desk names them rather than only counting them. A count agrees while the
::  pair underneath it has changed: rename one root and two is still two. So the guard
::  beside this desk reads both sides as SETS -- the roots written above and the marks
::  mark_verdict answers `.known` on -- and compares them sorted, then compares the count
::  to the desk's own list, to how many roots the engine publishes, and to how many it
::  answers on. The count is the fact a reader takes in at the door; the names are the
::  fact that keeps it honest.
+$  tilak-root-count-shape
  $:  roots=@u32
  ==
